+
+Servex writes `{"sent":{"to":"fast"|"smart","at":<iso>,"re":[<owner chat line at>…],"delay_ms":<n>}}` into the session log when it hands an owner line to the fast or the smart assistant (`mark_sent`). `to` says which assistant, `re` lists the owner lines it carried (their `chat.at`), `delay_ms` is how long after the line was said. Both views draw it as "fast ✓ 0.4 s · smart ✓ 3.1 s" (`sent_badge` in `ext/Chat/Chat.js`): the bubble chat under the owner bubble (`chat.js` passes it to `Widget.mark_sent`), Chat v2 under the Prompt whose owner `chat` line carries `prompt:"p-…"` (`ChatV2Model.apply` maps `re` to that Prompt). Proof: `test/chat-sent.mjs`.
